# 07 — Operator Overloading

## What is this?
Operator overloading allows custom classes to define behavior for standard operators like `+`, `==`, and `!=`.

## What to Practice
In `exercise.cpp`, implement class `Vector2D`:
- Fields: `int x`, `int y`.
- Constructor `Vector2D(int x = 0, int y = 0)`.
- Overload `Vector2D operator+(const Vector2D& other) const`
- Overload `bool operator==(const Vector2D& other) const`
- Overload `bool operator!=(const Vector2D& other) const`

## Reference Solution

<details>
<summary>Click to reveal reference solution</summary>

```cpp
class Vector2D {
public:
    int x;
    int y;

    Vector2D(int x_val = 0, int y_val = 0) : x(x_val), y(y_val) {}

    Vector2D operator+(const Vector2D& other) const {
        return Vector2D(x + other.x, y + other.y);
    }

    bool operator==(const Vector2D& other) const {
        return x == other.x && y == other.y;
    }

    bool operator!=(const Vector2D& other) const {
        return !(*this == other);
    }
};
```
</details>

